      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- TIP_DETAIL\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- range of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- variance of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- subjects offered by that department: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- departments that grant degrees: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- courses at the graduate level: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE_LEVEL\n- distinct subject IDs: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- minimum ISBN value: TIP_DETAIL.ISBN\n- course materials: TIP_DETAIL.ISBN\n- offering departments: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- offering schools: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME\n- number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- average number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, what is the range and variance of the number of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department, considering only departments that grant degrees and courses that are at the graduate level? Please provide the department name, the range of enrolled students, and the variance of enrolled students.\n```sql\nSELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) - MIN(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_range, VARIANCE(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_variance FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = scd.DEPARTMENT WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND scd.COURSE_LEVEL = 'G' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY enrolled_range DESC;\n```\n2. For each offering department name and school name where the number of enrolled students is greater than 2, provide the count of distinct subject IDs and the minimum ISBN value for the associated course materials.\n```sql\nSELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, tso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, COUNT(DISTINCT tso.SUBJECT_ID) AS subject_count, MIN(td.ISBN) AS min_isbn FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID WHERE tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 2 GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, tso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME;\n```\n3. For each department, what is the department name, the range of enrolled students, the variance of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department (considering only departments that grant degrees and courses at the graduate level), the count of distinct subject IDs, and the minimum ISBN value for the associated course materials (considering only offering departments and schools where the number of enrolled students is greater than 2)? Please provide the department name, the range of enrolled students, the variance of enrolled students, the count of distinct subject IDs, and the minimum ISBN value, in that order.\n```sql\nWITH DeptEnrolledStats AS ( SELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) - MIN(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_range, VARIANCE(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_variance FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = scd.DEPARTMENT WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND scd.COURSE_LEVEL = 'G' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY enrolled_range DESC ), DeptSubjectMaterialStats AS ( SELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, tso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, COUNT(DISTINCT tso.SUBJECT_ID) AS subject_count, MIN(td.ISBN) AS min_isbn FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID WHERE tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 2 GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, tso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME ) SELECT des.DEPARTMENT_NAME, des.enrolled_range, des.enrolled_variance, dsm.subject_count, dsm.min_isbn FROM DeptEnrolledStats des JOIN DeptSubjectMaterialStats dsm ON des.DEPARTMENT_NAME = dsm.OFFER_DEPT_NAME ORDER BY des.enrolled_range DESC;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each department, what is the department name, the range of enrolled students, the variance of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department (considering only departments that grant degrees and courses at the graduate level), the count of distinct subject IDs, the minimum ISBN value for the associated course materials (considering only offering departments and schools where the number of enrolled students is greater than 2), and the average number of enrolled students for those subjects? Please provide the department name, the range of enrolled students, the variance of enrolled students, the count of distinct subject IDs, the minimum ISBN value, and the average number of enrolled students, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers."
