mented column definitions exactly: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE; SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT ↔ SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID ↔ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (candidates for \"enrolled students\" measure):**\n| Candidate | Granularity | Enrollment column | ISBN available | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED | subject × term (textbook program) | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | via child TIP_DETAIL | table columns; dw_1165 SQL |\n| SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | section / subject × term (registrar) | enrollment numbers | no ISBN | concept_subject_offering_facts desc |\n| LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED | subject × term (library reserve) | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | reserve catalog ISBN only | table desc |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Range/variance of enrolled students for degree-granting depts + graduate courses → SUPPORTED only by TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (has NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS + OFFER_DEPT_CODE join to SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING and SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE_LEVEL); dw_1165 is a direct precedent. Registrar tables lack the documented join precedent for this exact shape.\n- Count distinct SUBJECT_ID + MIN(ISBN) where enrolled > 2 → SUPPORTED by TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ TIP_DETAIL (ISBN column exists only in TIP_DETAIL/TIP_MATERIAL/library catalog; hint anchors TIP_DETAIL.ISBN).\n- Average enrolled students \"for those subjects\" → SUPPORTED by AVG(TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) in the >2-enrolled population (column mapping: \"average number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\").\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"departments that grant degrees\" → SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' (department-level flag, per hint); \"courses at the graduate level\" → SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE_LEVEL = 'G' (documented value domain); \"the average number of enrolled